TI  - RAG Data Integrity Model: Hallucinations Are Architecture Failures
AB  - For CFOs and Board members: This framework answers the question "When does our AI investment start losing money?" in 5 minutes with 6 numbers. Most enterprise AI hallucination issues are not model problems — they are data architecture problems wearing a GenAI mask. When conflicting source records enter a vector index without upstream reconciliation, the RAG pipeline embeds all versions and outputs garbage. This piece reframes RAG hallucination as a data architecture failure and introduces the RAG Data Integrity Model: five failure modes (conflicting embeddings, stale embeddings, missing lineage, schema fragmentation, garbage semantics), each with root cause, symptom, and fix. Core principle: vector indexes are derived views, not sources of truth. They must be rebuilt when source data changes via CDC-triggered re-embedding pipelines. Data reconciliation must be enforced upstream from the embedding loop via data contracts at domain boundaries. Published April 2026. Licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. Keywords: RAG hallucination, retrieval augmented generation, AI hallucinations, vector database, data architecture, data integrity, embeddings, embedding drift, vector index staleness, data reconciliation, data contracts, CDC, RAG pipeline, enterprise AI, LLM.
