TI  - A Framework for Assessing and Mitigating Hallucination Risk in AI-Powered Cloud Banking and Blockchain Transactions
AB  - The integration of generative artificial intelligence into cloud banking and blockchain-based financial transactions promises substantial gains in efficiency and automation, yet introduces a critical and persistent reliability risk: model hallucination. Unlike deterministic systems, large language models (LLMs) generate outputs based on statistical pattern prediction rather than factual understanding, making them prone to producing confident but incorrect information—a phenomenon that in high-stakes financial contexts can lead to misinformed trading decisions, regulatory breaches, and significant financial losses . This paper proposes a comprehensive framework for assessing and mitigating hallucination risk in AI-powered financial systems operating at the intersection of cloud infrastructure, banking operations, and blockchain technology. The framework integrates a root cause-aware detection methodology—employing uncertainty estimation, semantic entropy analysis, and reasoning consistency checks—with a stratified mitigation strategy that combines knowledge grounding via retrieval-augmented generation, multi-model consensus mechanisms, and deterministic verification through automated reasoning . Drawing on empirical insights from recent industry pilots, including collaborations between Chainlink, Euroclear, Swift, and major financial institutions, we demonstrate how blockchain-based consensus frameworks and on-chain golden records can serve as trust anchors for validated AI outputs, reducing hallucination rates from over 14% to below 4% . The framework further addresses governance and regulatory alignment, proposing continuous supervisory overlays to complement traditional model risk management principles and accommodate the stochastic, nondeterministic nature of generative systems . By operationalizing hallucination management across model, data, and context tiers within a closed-loop continuous improvement cycle, this research provides financial institutions with a systematic, scalable methodology for deploying trustworthy generative AI in regulated, high-stakes environments.
